===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|fey||fated to die|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|fǣge||doomed to die, timid}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*faigijaz||cowardly, wicked}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*pAik-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*pAig-||ill-meaning, bad}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|fēgi}} whence {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|veeg||doomed, near death|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|feigi||appointed for death, ungodly|lang=goh}} whence {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|feige||cowardly|lang=de}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|feigr||doomed|lang=non}} whence the Icelandic {{term|feigur||doomed to die|lang=is}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|fāh||outlawed, hostile}}. More at {{l|en|foe}}.

